      annotations: [
        {
          id: 'a7.43.1',
          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g7.43.1'],
          lemma: "σχίσμα",
          title: "A division (σχίσμα) over him",
          body: "The word is **σχίσμα** — a *tearing, a split* (our “schism”), and it becomes a refrain wherever Jesus is present (9:16; 10:19). He does not leave a crowd neutral. The same words that draw some to faith harden others into hostility, and the line runs right through the middle of a people. This is judgment already happening (3:19; 9:39): light has come, and each person is sorted by how they answer it. Peace on his terms, or division — there is, in the end, no third response to him.",
        },
      ],
